{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06KC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)^{\\wedge}$", "MATH_0004": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\widehat{U}, \\widehat{R}, \\widehat{s}, \\widehat{t}, \\widehat{c})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-completion-groupoid-in-functors}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:952d9fbdca70772cba43c4a3da8c1024749fcad4973f9e7ff7d3987af4269864", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e9368685557b7aa01f2dc8a3a136e1623d2300573132d5c34e295f69dbb0a630", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a groupoid in functors on <MATH_0002>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>completion <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the\ngroupoid in functors\n<MATH_0005>\non <MATH_0006> described above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6a76611678d75c40a4538fdc60ec0141753c112a648fa7d534cfd838ece8548d", "unit_id": "tag:06KE:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06KC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)^{\\wedge}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda} \\cong (U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0006": "$U, R : \\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0007": "$U, R$", "MATH_0008": "$((U, R, s, t, c)|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda})^{\\wedge} \\cong (U, R, s, t, c)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-restrict-completion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-restrict-complete-continuous-functor}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-groupoid-in-functors-complete-restrict}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4c63d8e0dd2eff3df540f588c33333243cd895b68eeaa0f60c5f167838ec92f9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bd7df0878c218587a4d9b816b2121b3e51a2a6df9a37155ec5bb24cb23e5dbbd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a groupoid in functors on <MATH_0002>.\nThen there is a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0003>, see\nRemark <REF_0001>.\nOn the other hand, let <MATH_0004> be a groupoid in functors on\n<MATH_0005> such that\n<MATH_0006>\nboth commute with limits, e.g.<SPACE_0001>if <MATH_0007> are representable.\nThen there is a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0008>.\nThis follows from\nRemark <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ebaebb5cece35aaf457b157ace5807d02705ad4786517cad27e2021ffd08ae34", "unit_id": "tag:06KF:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06KC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-groupoid-in-functors-prorep-equivalences}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1a25285a052f6abf8f58a99bd96065edcaa8a4632e311d0563d2cf0fe8623a50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b9888a503f3dd3ec555515b11d83393cd2464337e9096d089174b208b1e6359b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a groupoid in functors on <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is prorepresentable if and only if its completion is\nrepresentable as a groupoid in functors on <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is prorepresentable if and only if <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> are\nprorepresentable.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9f0bdc264f9814cde72362fed3ea3d08807336e671008dcb6830813341d8f489", "unit_id": "tag:06KG:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06KC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\cong \\underline{R_0}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0004": "$R \\cong \\underline{R_1}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0005": "$R_0$", "MATH_0006": "$R_1$", "MATH_0007": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0008": "$\\underline{R_0} \\cong \\widehat{\\underline{R_0}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\underline{R_1} \\cong \\widehat{\\underline{R_1}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}}$", "MATH_0010": "$(U, R, s, t, c)^\\wedge$", "MATH_0011": "$(\\underline{R_0}, \\underline{R_1}, \\widehat{s}, \\widehat{t}, \\widehat{c})$", "MATH_0012": "$\\underline{R_1} \\times_{\\widehat{s}, \\underline{R_1}, \\widehat{t}}\n\\underline{R_1}$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\underline{R_0}, \\underline{R_1}, \\widehat{s}, \\widehat{t}, \\widehat{c})$", "MATH_0014": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0015": "$(\\underline{R_0}, \\underline{R_1}, s, t, c)|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0016": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0017": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-groupoid-in-functors-complete-restrict}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-restrict-complete-continuous-functor}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-CLambdahat-pushouts}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{remark-groupoid-in-functors-complete-restrict}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87048a85edf70e245537d09529e65ac06a178cb8d2d3f091f8a536523d92dd22", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a33118199720ad72af3a3524ce851789684b5a6abedde1df9b720678de5f335c", "source_text": "Part (1) follows from\nRemark <REF_0001>.\nFor (2), the ``only if'' direction is clear from the definition\nof a prorepresentable groupoid in functors. Conversely, assume <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>\nare prorepresentable, say <MATH_0003>\nand <MATH_0004> for objects <MATH_0005> and\n<MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007>.\nSince <MATH_0008>\nand <MATH_0009>\nby\nRemark <REF_0002>\nwe see that the completion <MATH_0010> is a groupoid in\nfunctors of the form\n<MATH_0011>.\nBy\nLemma <REF_0003>\nthe pushout\n<MATH_0012> exists. Hence\n<MATH_0013>\nis a representable groupoid in functors on <MATH_0014>.\nFinally, the restriction\n<MATH_0015>\ngives back <MATH_0016> by\nRemark <REF_0004>\nhence <MATH_0017> is prorepresentable by definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:35194450d7d1ade7aefd64d90200dcff0d363ffaf11b14993b636c8a6baa1a13", "unit_id": "tag:06KG:proof"}
